   "transcript": {
    "text": "Your company runs on training, hundreds of narrated courses, each frozen on the day it was recorded. Then something changes. Here, the Help Center now says to use the bookmark icon, not the heart. Drift Monitor flags every course that still teaches the old way. Rebuilding by hand means new captures, new edits, rebooking narration, and months behind every rollout. Now an agent reads the change and pins the exact line in each course that's out of date. It re-records just that line in the voice your learners already know. Then click the bookmark icon on the voice card to add it to Team Voices. Your team approves, and it's live in LMS, transcript, and all. Your team builds new programs instead of rebuilding old ones. Well said. Autopilot updates for legacy content.",
